{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And he made them a feast and unleavened breads, etc.</b> The meaning is that he made a feast in their honor, but they ate nothing except the matzot, for Lot did not fulfill the Torah as Abraham did. Therefore they did not wish to eat from the sacrifices of his feast as they ate from the calf that Abraham prepared — only the matzot. For the angels knew that he had separated his tithes and priestly gifts. Or it may be that since there were not yet any priests in the world, they themselves became priests and ate priestly gifts but not untithed produce. And according to the words of our Sages of blessed memory (Midrash HaGadol), it was the sixteenth of Nisan, and he fed them matzot; and since watchfulness is required, it was necessary to bake them by hand to guard them — and this is what the verse says <b>and unleavened breads he baked</b>:"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:42:18.594528424Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}